/obj/item/multitool/abductor{
	name = "Project-490 Multipurpose Interface";
	desc = "An abandoned ICW-era prototype from Johnson & Company's Industrial Supply division, meant to condense the various different control gadgets used by J&C's equipment, ranging from toasters to shipyard cranes, into one simple tool, with additional multitool capability able to determine the functions of wires, originally intended as an integrated tool for ARMS units. However, the cost of the project, combined with J&C's dire financial straits and the risk that M-W or the Coalition would try to seize such an advanced piece of kit for themselves, resulted in it being cancelled before actual production could begin, leaving this the only one of its kind. Right now, this multi-million-credit piece of Frontier history seems to be in use as a... television remote.";
